From 6dd6bbc86b405371f4329b1e5818c321b36d298e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 02:00:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] Per-client WebSocket presence + focus tracking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a single `/presence` WebSocket route owned by every connected
TUI for the life of its process. The connection itself is the
presence beacon — when the WebSocket closes (clean exit, SIGINT,
kill, network drop), the protocol's CLOSE frame triggers
`onClose` synchronously on the server and the entry is removed
from `_clients`. There is no batched-event problem because
WebSocket close detection lives below us in Bun's uSockets layer.

Focus updates ride on the same channel as JSON messages:

  client → server:  { "type": "focus", "sessionID": "ses_..." | null }

A single state mutation per navigation. No separate POST endpoint,
no client-generated UUIDs, no `X-Client-ID` header, no race between
the handshake and a follow-up focus call.

`_clients` keyed by `wsContext.raw` (the underlying ServerWebSocket)
because Hono wraps the raw socket in a fresh `WSContext` per
callback — using the wrapper as a Map key would fail lookups
between `onOpen` and subsequent callbacks.

Endpoints:
  - `GET /presence` (WebSocket upgrade) — the beacon.
  - `GET /global/live-sessions` — initial-seed reads. Returns
    `{ sessions: string[] }` (deduped focus values).

Bus event:
  - `session.live.changed` with payload `{ sessions: string[] }`.
    Published on every `_clients` mutation. The TUI footer's
    Sessions pill subscribes to this for live updates.

TUI (`sdk.tsx`):
  - Opens one `WebSocket` to `/presence` on mount.
  - `createEffect(route.data)` sends a focus message on every
    navigation. A small reconnect loop on `ws.close` for
    resilience; pendingFocus buffers the latest value until
    the new socket is open.

Footer (`feature-plugins/home/footer.tsx`):
  - Sessions pill: count = `event.properties.sessions.length`.
    Seeded from `GET /global/live-sessions` on mount.
  - Subagents pill: per-TUI, fetches
    `client.session.children(sessionID)` from the slot context.
    Refetches on `session.created` / `session.deleted` events
    whose `parentID` matches the focused session.
  - Drops the upstream `Directory` / `Mcp` / `Version` pills
    (the prior feedback that drove the cleanup).
  - Same View rendered into both `home_footer` and
    `session_footer` slots.

Tests: `packages/opencode/test/server/presence.test.ts` — seven
cases, all running native `Bun.serve` + real `WebSocket` clients:
focus appears, focus update mutates, blur to null, close removes
client, two-client kill-one only-drops-one, dedup on shared
session, malformed messages survive.

Drops the substrate complexity from the prior approach: no SSE
presence beacon, no `_subscriberCount` refcount, no Node http
event hooks (incoming/outgoing), no module-level sweep, no
active write probe, no socket setKeepAlive, no read-side flag
poll, no presence-related @hono/node-server dependence (already
gone from substrate commit). Net code: ~150 lines of presence
routes + ~50 lines TUI + ~250 lines tests, replacing what would
otherwise have been the 11-patch SSE iteration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
